You are an adversarial reviewer of scientific figures for a research proposal. The attached PNGs are rendered at 2x from SVG and will be displayed about 850 px wide. Try hard to find reasons each figure should not ship. For EACH image, by file order, report: (a) overlapping or colliding text, (b) lines or arrows that cross text or other arrows confusingly, (c) arrows whose direction or endpoints are ambiguous, (d) text too small to read at display size, (e) excess text that belongs in a caption, (f) the one main point and whether a reader gets it in 5 seconds, (g) concrete fixes with coordinates or element names. Then give a verdict per figure: ship / fix / redraw. Focus: Redrawn README overview figure (round 2). Single point: four places where a self-improving tool-using agent can go wrong, one per proposal: 05 the editable harness code, 07 the tool-output encoding the VLM reads, 08 the referral or hypothesis given to the agent, 06 the edit acceptance rule. Loop: scores on dev people, improver proposes an edit, candidate is scored, acceptance rule keeps or rejects, accepted edits change the code. Round 1 asked for a heading, uniform badges inside targets, input and output outside the editable frame, and an explicit scoring step.. Do not run commands or modify files.

